  "body": "Render posed vendor machine meshes in the `camcraft-sim` window (`#2587`) and provide a toggle against generated `#2584` blocks.\n\n## Context\nOnce local per-part machine meshes load through `#2591` and the display-chord loader, the standalone `camcraft-sim` viewer needs to display the posed vendor geometry and tell the operator clearly whether the active model is generated, visual-only (`not judged`), or solid.\n\n## Scope\n- Render loaded per-part vendor machine meshes at posed axis transforms inside `camcraft-sim` (`#2587`).\n- Add a display toggle in the viewer to switch between loaded vendor machine meshes and generated `#2584` blocks without restarting playback.\n- Show a visible status label that names whether the shown model is vendor solid, vendor visual-only (`not judged` for collision), or generated blocks (including when local files are absent).\n- Follow `crates/ui/AGENTS.md` for controls and AccessKit labels.\n\n## Done means\n`egui_kittest` tests in `crates/simview` render a multi-part posed vendor machine fixture across two axis poses without panic, toggle between vendor meshes and generated blocks, and assert the visual-only and generated status labels.\n\nDepends on #2587 and #2591.\n\nPart of #3239\n",
